Don't let printenv find a name that contains '='.
getenv() compares the name with the start of each environment entry,
so with FOO set to "a=b", "printenv FOO=a" matched it and printed the
value, or what followed the extra '=', and exited 0. No variable name
contains '=', so treat such a name as not set, as coreutils does.

---
 coreutils/printenv.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/printenv.c
+++ b/coreutils/printenv.c
@@ -47,7 +47,8 @@
 		char *arg, *env;
 
 		while ((arg = *++argv) != NULL) {
-			env = getenv(arg);
+			/* getenv("A=b") can match the variable A=b=c */
+			env = strchr(arg, '=') ? NULL : getenv(arg);
 			if (env)
 				puts(env);
 			else
